From: 6a0 <87043474+6a0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 127/128] glm cuda: a shared window's sampled streams draw
 after one gather and one sync (TF_GLM_DRAW_BATCH=0: each alone)

A shared verify window whose streams all decode greedily takes one pick launch, one gather, one sync and one
read. With a sampled stream in it (temperature over 0: served traffic) every part ran Engine.draw on its own:
its rows copied whole, a group of NCCL broadcasts, two uploads, tf_draw, a synchronize and a read, a stream,
one after the other behind the forward. Now, when every part is sampled and no grammar is in the step, all the
window's rows go whole in one gather (one group), each part's tf_draw launches on its rows of that buffer under
its own rule and positions (Sampler.drawParts), and one synchronize and one read end the step; the other ranks
join the one gather as they joined each part's. A step with a grammar or a greedy stream beside sampled ones
draws as before.

The same kernel on the same rows with the same rule and position keys: the same tokens. Not compiled or run
here (no toolchain on the serving host).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_engine.zig  | 23 ++++++++++++++++++-
 zig/src/families/glm/cuda_sampler.zig | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
